repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Amrs03/A-Systematic-Review-and-Comparative-Analysis-of-Arabic-Centric-SOTA-Language-Models-Code
abstract: >-
  Evaluation pipeline, result artifacts, and CPU-only reproducibility audit for
  a two-track comparative study of five Arabic-centric language models (ALLaM,
  Falcon-Arabic, JAIS, MARBERT, AraBERT) on a single 8 GB consumer GPU. Track A
  fine-tunes two compact encoders on five Arabic understanding datasets; Track B
  evaluates four instruction-tuned decoders zero-shot on six multiple-choice
  benchmarks. The audit re-derives every reported number from the surviving
  artifacts and shows that only 2 of 23 completed decoder runs are capability
  measurements, the remainder being determined by harness defects in gold-label
  lookup, prompt construction, decode budget, and answer extraction.
keywords:
  - Arabic natural language processing
  - large language models
  - benchmarking
  - evaluation
